course: dictionary
lesson: 10685
title: Unpredictably
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Unpredictably means in a way that cannot be guessed or known before it happens. Predict means to say what will happen before it does, and un- means not, so unpredictable things are hard to forecast.
explain: «The weather in the mountains changes unpredictably, so hikers always pack a warm coat.» You cannot know if it will rain, snow or be sunny at any moment. The clue is in the word: the change cannot be planned for.
explain: Animals and people can act unpredictably too. «The puppy ran unpredictably around the garden» means you could not guess which way it would turn next. To check, swap in a meaning: "in a way nobody could guess." If it still makes sense, you have it.
fact: Unpredictably means in a way that cannot be guessed before it happens.
fact: The adjective is unpredictable, and the adverb is unpredictably.
fact: «The weather changed unpredictably all afternoon» means the sky kept changing in ways nobody could expect.
fact: Weather, animals and people's moods can all behave unpredictably.
fact: In maths, one dice roll is unpredictable, but after many rolls a pattern appears.
exercise: «The weather in the hills changes unpredictably.» What does unpredictably mean? | In a warm and sunny way | In a loud and noisy way | In a slow and steady way | *In a way nobody can guess beforehand
exercise: A dice roll behaves unpredictably. Why? | It never lands flat | It always shows a six | It is too heavy to roll | *Nobody can know the number before it lands
exercise: «The puppy ran unpredictably around the garden.» Find and copy the adverb. | garden | *unpredictably | around | ran
test: Which word is the adjective form of unpredictably? | predictable | *unpredictable | predicting | predictor
test: «The storm arrived unpredictably.» What does this suggest? | It was very quiet | *It came at a time nobody could guess | It was planned weeks ahead | It happened at the same time every day
exam: Which sentence uses unpredictably correctly? | The sum is 2 plus 2, unpredictably. | *The kitten leapt unpredictably from the sofa to the curtains. | The dice always lands on six, so it rolls unpredictably. | The bus arrives at exactly 8:15 every morning, so it is unpredictably.
